{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["And the man gazed — from the root of תשאה שממה, and the tav is like the tav in ישתבח from שבח, and ישתמר חקות עמרי from שמר, meaning: astonished and pondering what this girl said to him. And one who explains it as deriving from drinking is impossible, because the alef in it would not occur in a form from drinking. Furthermore, Rivqah did not say to him to water his camels until after he had drunk, and only then did he begin to ponder and wonder."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The alef argument: the form משתאה contains an alef, whereas a hitpa'el of שתה (to drink) would not; therefore it cannot mean 'was drinking'."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:57.612445930Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}